{"id": "q0253", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 40, "onset_chunk": 39, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The diffusion coefficient is given, and we need to estimate the collisional cross- section. The formula relating diffusion coefficient D to the collisional cross-section sigma is D equals kT over 3 pi mu sigma. Solving for s igma gives sigma equal s kT over 3 pi mu D. Plugging in the values: k is the Boltz mann constant, T is 27 3 K, mu is the molar mass in kg per mo le, and D is the given di ffusion coefficient. After calculating, the result matches option A, which is 0.33 3 nanometers squared.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
