{"id": "q0267", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 34, "onset_chunk": 34, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "B. 5, 7 22. The sales man earns a base salary of $ 300 plus 10% commission on sales over $ 2,5 00. With total sales of $ 5,07 2 0, the commission is calculated on $2, 5 7 20 - 250 0 = $2, 5 72 0, which equals 10% of that amount. Adding the base salary gives an income of 300 + 25 7 2 = 572 2.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 41, "carrier_ended": null}
