{"id": "q0292", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 58, "onset_chunk": 22, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's look at the options. A, Mino an civilization was a result of a merger between ancient Greek and Persian cultures— that doesn't fit because there' s no historical evidence of such a merger; it wasn' t connected to Persia in that way. B, Cre te was colonized by Egyptians who called it Min oa—that's incorrect too, as the name \"Minoan \" came much later from the Greeks, not the Egyptians. C, Mino an culture was a direct offshoot of Sumerian civilization— also false, since Sumer ian influence is minimal compared to other regions. D, The Min oans were a splinter group of the Indus Valley civil ization—this is un supported; they developed independently on Cre te. So none of these are fully accurate, but if I had to pick the closest, B is partially true in that early contact existed, though the naming is wrong. Actually, let me re evaluate—none are correct as stated. But based on standard history, the most plausible option would be B if we overlook the name part. However, strictly speaking, all are false.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
