{"id": "q0379", "pool": "easy-fact", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In Roman mythology, the god of war was Mars. He was a central figure in Roman religion and culture, often depicted with a spear or carrying weapons like a shield. The month of March is named after him, and he played a significant role in many Roman myths and ritual s related to battle and conquest.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
