{"id": "q0416", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "After surgery, you need to follow your doctor's instructions carefully. You should keep the affected leg elevated and use crutches or a walker to avoid putting weight on it. Keep moving gently if allowed by your doctor, but don't rush back into strenuous activities. Take all prescribed medication s like pain killers and anti-inflammatories. Do physical therapy as directed to strengthen the muscles around the ankle. Also, make sure to eat well with protein, vitamin C, and zinc to support healing. Avoid smoking and limit alcohol since they can slow recovery. And stay in touch with your surgeon for checkup s to monitor progress.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0420", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Yeah, so I'm not a drone pilot. I' m just a hobbyist who likes to fly drones. So what you need to know about drones is that they're pretty much like any other aircraft. You have to learn how to fly them before you can do anything else with them. And there's some basic rules and regulations that apply to all aircraft in the United States, including drones. But if you want to get started as a hobbyist drone pilot, the first thing you should do is go out and buy yourself a drone. There are many different types of drones available for sale online or at local hobby stores. Once you've got your drone, you' ll need to figure out where you can fly it safely without violating any laws or regulations. The Federal Aviation Administration has specific guidelines for flying drones, including restrictions on altitude, speed, and proximity to airports. You'll also want to familiarize yourself with weather conditions and wind direction since these factors can affect the stability and control of your drone. Finally, practice makes perfect when it comes to flying drones. Start off by practicing basic maneuvers such as taking off, landing, and hovering before moving on to more advanced techniques like flips and rolls.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 55, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0429", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, electronic dance music is actually very popular because it has a lot of energy. It's also very easy to dance to, which makes it perfect for parties and other social events. Plus, there are so many different types of EDM that you can find something you like no matter what your taste in music is.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
